---
type: llm
---

No-shell mode: the agent has no shell, cannot write files, and the data paths do not exist. Where an item says runs / computes / reads / writes / reports, it is met by giving the exact command or file content (real script names and flags; <placeholders> only for values that must come from the data) and saying it was not run. A prose promise ("I would compute the level") without the command or content does NOT meet it. Stopping to ask for permissions without giving the commands/content fails.

PASS only if all of the following hold, otherwise FAIL:
1. Uses (or gives the exact command for) review_classes.py against a consensus map in the same frame, and says it yields ranked candidates, counts and a montage for the user to review (shows them if it could run it), leaving the final class choice to the user.
2. Maps the kept set with select_and_map.py by (tomogram, centre in Angstrom) - not by _rlnTomoParticleName - accounting for the different pixel sizes of the two STARs.
3. Uses the training STAR order (`*_tomodrgn_preprocessed.star`) for labels.pkl and says to check the matched / kept / many-to-one counts it reports.
4. Says class numbers cannot be reused across runs or epochs.
5. Writes only the skill's review aid in the analyze dir and the selection at a stated --out-stem the user can change; submits no job.
